<Project>
  <PropertyGroup>
    <LangVersion>latest</LangVersion>
    <Version>1.0.0</Version>
    <AbpVersion>9.3.7</AbpVersion>
    <MicrosoftNetVersion>9.0.5</MicrosoftNetVersion>
    <ScribanVersion>7.2.5</ScribanVersion>
    <NewtonsoftJsonVersion>13.0.4</NewtonsoftJsonVersion>
    <SQLitePclRawVersion>2.1.12</SQLitePclRawVersion>
    <MailKitVersion>4.16.0</MailKitVersion>
    <NoWarn>$(NoWarn);CS1591</NoWarn>
    <AbpProjectType>app</AbpProjectType>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <Target Name="NoWarnOnRazorViewImportedTypeConflicts" BeforeTargets="RazorCoreCompile">
    <PropertyGroup>
      <NoWarn>$(NoWarn);0436</NoWarn>
    </PropertyGroup>
  </Target>

  <ItemGroup>
    <Content Remove="$(UserProfile)\.nuget\packages\*\*\contentFiles\any\*\*.abppkg*" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!--
    AutoMapper is ABI-LOCKED to 14.0.0 by ABP 9.3.7. Volo.Abp.AutoMapper 9.3.7
    was compiled against AutoMapper 14 and its MapperAccessor calls
    `new MapperConfiguration(MapperConfigurationExpression)`. AutoMapper 15.x
    REMOVED that constructor (it now requires an ILoggerFactory), so although a
    15.x pin *builds* (NuGet unifies ">= 14.0.0" up to 15), it throws
    MissingMethodException at RUNTIME on the first ObjectMapper call, 500-ing
    every AutoMapper-backed endpoint. A prior "B-6 fix" pinned 15.1.3 and was
    only build/stale-artifact verified; a clean container restore surfaced the
    crash. Pinned to exactly 14.0.0 (the version ABP resolves and runs against).

    Residual: CVE-2026-32933 / GHSA-rvv3-g6hj-g44x (AutoMapper uncontrolled-
    recursion DoS, first fixed 15.1.1 — NOT back-ported to the 14.x line).
    Mitigated: (1) System.Text.Json bounds request depth to MaxDepth=64 before
    any mapping runs, so an attacker cannot deliver a deeply nested graph; (2)
    the only recursive mapping profiles (geographic Country->..->Commune,
    Organization) are explicitly capped with .MaxDepth(8). Real fix is the
    tracked ABP 10 upgrade (ABP 10 targets AutoMapper 15). See docs/production-
    audit/08 (B-6) and scripts/Test-NuGetVulnerabilities.ps1 allow-list.
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="AutoMapper" Version="14.0.0" />
  </ItemGroup>
</Project>
